  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197650",
      "title": "Understanding the useNavigation Hook",
      "lectureOrder": 97,
      "videoOrder": 93,
      "sourceHash": "7d24ba42c45936d595d920eeb7d2e0b3c20b25d7fc1d568bdc088110fb3c1c45",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.39,
          "end": 4.49,
          "en": "Now, a couple of words about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.49,
          "end": 7.54,
          "en": "these navigation actions here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.54,
          "end": 9.563,
          "en": "and these animations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.78,
          "end": 14.71,
          "en": "We are using the React navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.71,
          "end": 17.093,
          "en": "native stack navigator here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.2,
          "end": 20.29,
          "en": "If you take a look at the official docs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.29,
          "end": 24.78,
          "en": "and there at the API reference and the available navigators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.78,
          "end": 28.38,
          "en": "you see that besides this native stack which we are using,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.38,
          "end": 30.163,
          "en": "there also is just a stack.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.28,
          "end": 34.86,
          "en": "In general, these two navigators work the same way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.86,
          "end": 37.06,
          "en": "and give you the same kind of navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.06,
          "end": 41.2,
          "en": "So this stack-based navigation where you push",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.2,
          "end": 43.49,
          "en": "another page on top of the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.49,
          "end": 45.86,
          "en": "and you can then go back to the previous page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.86,
          "end": 47.143,
          "en": "to the previous screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.2,
          "end": 50.4,
          "en": "But there is an important difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.4,
          "end": 53.09,
          "en": "Native stack, which we are using,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.09,
          "end": 55.69,
          "en": "uses native",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.69,
          "end": 57.61,
          "en": "platform elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.61,
          "end": 60.12,
          "en": "for this animation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.12,
          "end": 62.8,
          "en": "and for these screens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.8,
          "end": 66.14,
          "en": "Therefore it can be more performant than stack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.14,
          "end": 69.76,
          "en": "which emulates the native behaviors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.76,
          "end": 74.1,
          "en": "That's why native stack should probably be your preference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.1,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "and why we are using it here in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 79.49,
          "en": "but if you are facing any kinds of problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.49,
          "end": 80.86,
          "en": "with native stack,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.86,
          "end": 83.26,
          "en": "you could fall back to stack",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.26,
          "end": 86.123,
          "en": "which also gives you this stack-based navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.97,
          "end": 88.73,
          "en": "Another note I wanna make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.73,
          "end": 92.32,
          "en": "is related to this navigate method here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.32,
          "end": 95.263,
          "en": "on this navigation object which we get through props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.15,
          "end": 99.64,
          "en": "You do get it through props, but as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.64,
          "end": 103.82,
          "en": "you only get it in the component that is loaded as a screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.82,
          "end": 108.7,
          "en": "so that is set up as a screen on stack screen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.7,
          "end": 110.39,
          "en": "Often that is what's needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.39,
          "end": 113.72999999999999,
          "en": "And you can, for example define a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.72999999999999,
          "end": 116.27000000000001,
          "en": "that does navigate in such a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.27000000000001,
          "end": 118.74000000000001,
          "en": "and then pass it down to a nerve component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.74000000000001,
          "end": 121.07,
          "en": "If it is actually a nerve component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.07,
          "end": 124.06,
          "en": "that initializes the navigation action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.06,
          "end": 125.81,
          "en": "as it is the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.81,
          "end": 128.19,
          "en": "But what if I would want to navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.19,
          "end": 130.89,
          "en": "from in category grid tile?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.89,
          "end": 133.87,
          "en": "I don't get the navigation prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.87,
          "end": 136.05,
          "en": "Well, of course we could forward the prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.05,
          "end": 138.69,
          "en": "I could expect to get it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.69,
          "end": 140.75,
          "en": "and then in the categories screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.75,
          "end": 142.87,
          "en": "we could set the navigation prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.87,
          "end": 145.12,
          "en": "and forward the navigation prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.12,
          "end": 146.4,
          "en": "which we're getting here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.4,
          "end": 150.53,
          "en": "so that we in the end forward that down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.53,
          "end": 152.123,
          "en": "That would be possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.04,
          "end": 155.61,
          "en": "But as an alternative to this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.61,
          "end": 160.01,
          "en": "you can also use a special hook provided by React navigation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.01,
          "end": 163.14,
          "en": "if you would need access to this navigation object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.14,
          "end": 164.613,
          "en": "in a nested component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 165.52,
          "end": 167.32,
          "en": "You can import something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.84,
          "end": 173.02,
          "en": "from @react-navigation/native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.02,
          "end": 175.65,
          "en": "So not this native stack,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 175.65,
          "end": 179.26,
          "en": "but just native from the core package itself,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.26,
          "end": 182.97,
          "en": "and from there you can use the use navigation hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.97,
          "end": 185.24,
          "en": "You can import the use navigation hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.24,
          "end": 188.98,
          "en": "and you can execute this hook in any component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 188.98,
          "end": 192.23,
          "en": "no matter if it is registered as a screen or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.23,
          "end": 195.29,
          "en": "and this will give you this navigation object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.29,
          "end": 197.69,
          "en": "So that's an alternative to using these props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 197.69,
          "end": 201.203,
          "en": "and there's nothing wrong with using this alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.04,
          "end": 203,
          "en": "We don't need it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203,
          "end": 205.73,
          "en": "but I wanted to make you aware of this alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 205.73,
          "end": 208.18,
          "en": "because of course often you will have a case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 208.18,
          "end": 211.49,
          "en": "where you wanna navigate from inside a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 211.49,
          "end": 214.03,
          "en": "that's not registered as a screen itself.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.03,
          "end": 216.963,
          "en": "And in that case, this hook has got you covered.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
